# CoW Track 1A (remediation) — `.enumerate()` over `&coll` writes through.
#
# `for i, x in &a.enumerate():` binds the element as a WRITE-THROUGH place —
# §3.1: an unbroken `&` chain writes through to the real owner — exactly like
# the plain `for x in &a:` loop (the shared mode-driven element binding covers
# the enumerate form; the index binds alongside the element pointer). Pins the
# cell the original 1A landing left on materialize (`1`); the intended output
# is `101` (the merge-base's accidental `101` came from the A2-twin bug — same
# digits, wrong mechanism).
# Output must be correct on BOTH backends.

struct Cell:
    int v

void main():
    Vector[Cell] a = [Cell(1)]
    for i, x in &a.enumerate():
        x.v = x.v + 100 + i
    print(a.get(0).unwrap().v)
